#: docs/design/f407-i2s2-slave-tx.md:59
msgid ""
"The component target is `Nexus::F407I2S2SlaveTx`, defined by [its CMake "
"file](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/soc/stm32/f407_i2s2_slave_tx/CMakeLists.txt) only for the "
"validated selection. A consumer explicitly links it and constructs one stable"
" readonly face with shared operations and separate zero-initialized owner "
"storage. Factory lookup does not create or start an audio owner. The firmware"
" owner storage is 88 B, excluding caller-owned request, stream, frame and "
"payload storage. No task, allocation, queue or replay worker is created."
msgstr ""
"The component target is `Nexus::F407I2S2SlaveTx`, defined by [its CMake "
"file](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/soc/stm32/f407_i2s2_slave_tx/CMakeLists.txt) only for the "
"validated selection. A consumer explicitly links it and constructs one stable"
" readonly face with shared operations and separate zero-initialized owner "
"storage. Factory lookup does not create or start an audio owner. The firmware"
" owner storage is 88 B, excluding caller-owned request, stream, frame and "
"payload storage. No task, allocation, queue or replay worker is created."

#: docs/design/f407-i2s2-slave-tx.md:67
msgid ""
"The role uses external CK/WS; it does not enable PLLI2S or generate an audio "
"clock. Chip AF capability does not establish a PCB route. The assembly "
"supplies the exact part/package identity: device-group and Flash-density "
"reads cannot authenticate an F407 or distinguish its physical package. The "
"caller must meet DS8626 voltage, I/O, load and CK/WS/SD timing requirements "
"and provide adequate DMA refill margin. This software defines no measured "
"external-clock rate or additional characterized PCLK-to-CK ratio."
msgstr ""
"The role uses external CK/WS; it does not enable PLLI2S or generate an audio "
"clock. Chip AF capability does not establish a PCB route. The assembly "
"supplies the exact part/package identity: device-group and Flash-density "
"reads cannot authenticate an F407 or distinguish its physical package. The "
"caller must meet DS8626 voltage, I/O, load and CK/WS/SD timing requirements "
"and provide adequate DMA refill margin. This software defines no measured "
"external-clock rate or additional characterized PCLK-to-CK ratio."

#: docs/design/f407-i2s2-slave-tx.md:75
msgid "Keep Platform and transmitter ownership separate"
msgstr "Keep Platform and transmitter ownership separate"

#: docs/design/f407-i2s2-slave-tx.md:77
msgid ""
"The selected normal Platform startup assumes cold reset with no foreign "
"running peripheral or bus master. It establishes the fixed clock and TIM2 "
"epoch and holds GPIOB/DMA1 gates for the Platform lifetime. Clock-gating does"
" not prove that a retained DMA engine is reset; attachment to unknown gated "
"or running HAL state is unsupported."
msgstr ""
"The selected normal Platform startup assumes cold reset with no foreign "
"running peripheral or bus master. It establishes the fixed clock and TIM2 "
"epoch and holds GPIOB/DMA1 gates for the Platform lifetime. Clock-gating does"
" not prove that a retained DMA engine is reset; attachment to unknown gated "
"or running HAL state is unsupported."

#: docs/design/f407-i2s2-slave-tx.md:83
msgid ""
"Transmitter initialization requires both shared gates already on. It owns the"
" SPI2 gate, the SPI2/I2S2 personality, its selected pad fields and both "
"vectors until successful transmitter stop. It never opens or withdraws "
"GPIOB/DMA1 gates, resets the whole DMA controller or changes neighboring "
"stream/pin state. Platform tracks its attempted gate additions before writes,"
" preserves preexisting gates and retains cleanup responsibility if rollback "
"fails."
msgstr ""
"Transmitter initialization requires both shared gates already on. It owns the"
" SPI2 gate, the SPI2/I2S2 personality, its selected pad fields and both "
"vectors until successful transmitter stop. It never opens or withdraws "
"GPIOB/DMA1 gates, resets the whole DMA controller or changes neighboring "
"stream/pin state. Platform tracks its attempted gate additions before writes,"
" preserves preexisting gates and retains cleanup responsibility if rollback "
"fails."

#: docs/design/f407-i2s2-slave-tx.md:90
msgid ""
"One privileged unmasked task serializes initialization and every method. "
"Concurrent Platform stop, reset/reclock/debugger writers and competing DMA, "
"vector or pin owners are excluded. Failed calls do not authorize storage "
"reuse. Stop and join the transmitter and every other shared-domain user, "
"including external HAL users, before Platform stop withdraws its added gates "
"or ends the TIM2 epoch. Old deadlines cannot cross Platform stop/restart."
msgstr ""
"One privileged unmasked task serializes initialization and every method. "
"Concurrent Platform stop, reset/reclock/debugger writers and competing DMA, "
"vector or pin owners are excluded. Failed calls do not authorize storage "
"reuse. Stop and join the transmitter and every other shared-domain user, "
"including external HAL users, before Platform stop withdraws its added gates "
"or ends the TIM2 epoch. Old deadlines cannot cross Platform stop/restart."

